skill: "freelancer-operations"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# Freelancer Operations System\n\nRun your freelance practice like a lean, profitable business — not a chaotic side-hustle. This module covers the financial, legal, and operational infrastructure that keeps revenue flowing, risk controlled, time protected, and growth systematic.\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Skill Architecture\n\nTo utilize this skill's financial sheets, legal templates, or tool checklists, read the corresponding document in the `references/` directory:\n\n| File | Focus | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| [06A-FINANCE-TRACKING.md](references/06A-FINANCE-TRACKING.md) | Finance & Invoicing | Dedicated business banking setup, Wise/Payoneer setup, invoicing fields, international payment routes, tax reserves, expense tracking spreadsheet structure |\n| [06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md](references/06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md) | Legal & Contracts | 12 essential contract clauses, IP assignment, NDA terms, non-solicitation, payment penalty terms, governing law selection |\n| [06C-AUTOMATION-STACK.md](references/06C-AUTOMATION-STACK.md) | Automation Stack | Zero-maintenance CRM design, Zapier/Make/n8n comparison, AI-assisted lead parsing and onboarding automations |\n| [06D-TIME-MANAGEMENT.md](references/06D-TIME-MANAGEMENT.md) | Time Management | Deep work architecture, calendar blocking, IST/global time zone scheduling, asynchronous communication boundary scripts |\n| [06E-SCALING-SYSTEMS.md](references/06E-SCALING-SYSTEMS.md) | Scaling Systems | Productized service design, premium retainer models, digital products, hiring sub-contractors, solo-to-agency flywheel |\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Agent Guidelines & Workflows\n\n"
  - "### 1. Financial Infrastructure & Invoicing\nWhen asked to set up or audit a freelancer's financial workflow:\n- Reference [06A-FINANCE-TRACKING.md](references/06A-FINANCE-TRACKING.md) to split incoming revenue: 30% for taxes, 20% for business development, 50% for owner salary/expenses.\n- Guide the freelancer to set up Wise or Payoneer for international client transactions to minimize conversion fees.\n- Design clean invoices containing all legally required fields.\n\n"
  - "### 2. Legal Contracts & Clauses\nWhen drafting or reviewing client contracts:\n- Reference [06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md](references/06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md) to verify that the contract includes the **12 Essential Clauses** (IP Assignment upon final payment, late payment penalties, clear termination terms, and governing jurisdiction).\n- Advise on NDA boundaries to protect the freelancer's background IP (boilerplates, reusable utilities).\n\n"
  - "### 3. CRM & Operational Automation\nWhen designing an automated admin workflow:\n- Reference [06C-AUTOMATION-STACK.md](references/06C-AUTOMATION-STACK.md) to choose the correct automation framework (Zapier, Make, or self-hosted n8n).\n- Set up the **CRM Lead Capture Engine**: Typeform/Cal.com $\\rightarrow$ n8n/Zapier $\\rightarrow$ Slack $\\rightarrow$ Airtable.\n\n"
  - "### 4. Time Defense & Calendars\nWhen auditing calendar schedules or time-management practices:\n- Reference [06D-TIME-MANAGEMENT.md](references/06D-TIME-MANAGEMENT.md) to structure a calendar using **Deep Work Architecture** (blocking 3-4 hour uninterrupted periods for coding, separating client calls to specific afternoons).\n- Formulate async-first email or Slack boundaries to block constant client interruptions.\n\n"
  - "### 5. Scaling Beyond Freelancing\nWhen asked to scale operations, raise prices, or hire team members:\n- Reference [06E-SCALING-SYSTEMS.md](references/06E-SCALING-SYSTEMS.md) to productize complex services (e.g., \"ML model audit for $2,500\" with a fixed scope, clear inputs, and standardized outputs).\n- Structure sub-contracting agreements to delegate basic tasks while preserving quality control.\n\n---\n\n"
  - "## Quick Reference Summary\n\n| Concept | File | Section | One-Line Summary |\n|---------|------|---------|------------------|\n| The 50/30/20 Rule | [06A](references/06A-FINANCE-TRACKING.md) | 2.1 | Allocate income: 50% Salary/Operating, 30% Tax Reserve, 20% Growth Fund |\n| IP Protection Clause | [06B](references/06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md) | 2.1 | Ensure intellectual property only transfers to the client *after* the final invoice is paid |\n| Late Payment Penalty | [06B](references/06B-LEGAL-CONTRACTS.md) | 2.4 | Protect cash flow by enforcing a 1.5% monthly interest fee on overdue invoices |\n| CRM Automation | [06C](references/06C-AUTOMATION-STACK.md) | 3 | Automate: Web Form Lead $\\rightarrow$ parser $\\rightarrow$ calendar book $\\rightarrow$ Slack alert |\n| Deep Work Blocks | [06D](references/06D-TIME-MANAGEMENT.md) | 2 | Schedule 4-hour morning blocks with all notifications disabled |\n| Productized Services | [06E](references/06E-SCALING-SYSTEMS.md) | 1.1 | Move from hourly billing to standardized, fixed-scope packages |\n\n---\n\n> **Previous Skill:** [freelancer-post-delivery ←](../freelancer-post-delivery/SKILL.md)\n> **Next Skill:** [freelancer-developer-resources →](../freelancer-developer-resources/SKILL.md)\n"
